<entry key="group|hint|GR-Lot-ProcurementType">This section refers to the use of public procurement to achieve broader policy objectives in addition to purchasing works, supplies or services, such as environmental sustainability, social responsibility, innovation and SME participation. The directives regulate this approach through provisions allowing environmental, social and innovation-related criteria in technical specifications, award criteria and contract performance conditions.</entry>
<entry key="group|hint|GR-LotResult-ReceivedSubmissions">In this section, you must indicate the number of received tenders, whether they were submitted electronically, whether they were received from SMEs, and whether they originated from within or outside the EEA. This information is mandatory for each lot result when the lot is awarded. You can also optionally indicate other types of submissions, such as the number of requests to participate received during the first stage of the procedure or the number and nature of any inadmissible tenders. You must add a section for each type and number of submissions.</entry>
<entry key="group|hint|GR-LotResult-Section">This section contains information on the award of a lot. You can indicate whether the lot was awarded, identify the winning and non-winning tenders, and provide the reference of the contract that was signed.</entry>
<entry key="group|hint|GR-Procedure-LocalLegalBasisWithID">The legal basis can be identified using its ELI (European Legislation Identifier) or its CELEX number, as used by EUR-Lex: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/content/help/eurlex-content/celex-number.html?locale=en</entry>
<entry key="group|hint|GR-Procedure-PlaceOfPerformance">This section defines the main location of works or the main place of delivery or performance for supplies and services, which can be defined at the relevant level: anywhere in the world, anywhere in the EEA, anywhere in a specific country, within a specific country subdivision (NUTS code), or at a specific location or address. You can add more sections if you need to define more than one country, subdivision or address.</entry>
<entry key="group|hint|GR-Withheld-Notice">This section allows you to withhold one or more groups of fields from being published. You must specify a reason for not disclosing the information and you may also provide further information. If you do not provide a disclosure date, the undisclosed fields will never be published, otherwise you can provide a date up to 5 years in the future and your notice will be published again and disclosing the information. More information is available at https://ted.europa.eu/en/simap/undisclosed</entry>
